      <h2 id="using-data-protection-test_oadp-data-protection-test" class="group scroll-mt-20">Using the DataProtectionTest custom resource<a href="#using-data-protection-test_oadp-data-protection-test" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1">&para;</a></h2>
      <p class="_abstract">Configure and run the <code>DataProtectionTest</code> (DPT) custom resource (CR) to verify Container Storage Interface (CSI) snapshot readiness and data upload performance to your storage bucket. This helps you validate your OADP environment before performing backup and restore operations.</p>
      <p><strong>Prerequisites</strong></p>
      <ul>
      <li>You have logged in to the OpenShift Container Platform cluster as a user with the <code>cluster-admin</code> role.</li>
      <li>You have installed the OpenShift CLI (<code>oc</code>).</li>
      <li>You have installed the OADP Operator.</li>
      <li>You have created the <code>DataProtectionApplication</code> (DPA) CR.</li>
      <li>You have configured a backup storage location (BSL) to store the backups.</li>
      <li>You have an application with persistent volume claims (PVCs) running in a separate namespace.</li>
      </ul>
      <p><strong>Procedure</strong></p>
      <ol>
      <li>
      Create a manifest file for the DPT CR as shown in the example:
      <CodeBlock code={"apiVersion: oadp.openshift.io/v1alpha1\nkind: DataProtectionTest\nmetadata:\n  name: dpt-sample\n  namespace: openshift-adp\nspec:\n  backupLocationName: <bsl_name>\n  csiVolumeSnapshotTestConfigs:\n  - snapshotClassName: csi-gce-pd-vsc\n    timeout: 90s\n    volumeSnapshotSource:\n      persistentVolumeClaimName: <pvc1_name>\n      persistentVolumeClaimNamespace: <pvc_namespace>\n  - snapshotClassName: csi-gce-pd-vsc\n    timeout: 120s\n    volumeSnapshotSource:\n      persistentVolumeClaimName: <pvc2_name>\n      persistentVolumeClaimNamespace: <pvc_namespace>\n  forceRun: false\n  uploadSpeedTestConfig:\n    fileSize: 200MB\n    timeout: 120s"} lang="yaml" />
      <p>where:</p>
      <dl class="my-4 space-y-2">
      <dt class="font-semibold"><code>&lt;bsl_name&gt;</code></dt>
      <dd class="ml-6 text-muted-foreground"><p>Specifies the name of the BSL.</p></dd>
      <dt class="font-semibold"><code>csiVolumeSnapshotTestConfigs</code></dt>
      <dd class="ml-6 text-muted-foreground"><p>Specifies a list for <code>csiVolumeSnapshotTestConfigs</code>. In this example, two PVCs are being tested.</p></dd>
      <dt class="font-semibold"><code>&lt;pvc1_name&gt;</code></dt>
      <dd class="ml-6 text-muted-foreground"><p>Specifies the name of the first PVC.</p></dd>
      <dt class="font-semibold"><code>&lt;pvc_namespace&gt;</code></dt>
      <dd class="ml-6 text-muted-foreground"><p>Specifies the namespace of the PVC.</p></dd>
      <dt class="font-semibold"><code>&lt;pvc2_name&gt;</code></dt>
      <dd class="ml-6 text-muted-foreground"><p>Specifies the name of the second PVC.</p></dd>
      <dt class="font-semibold"><code>forceRun</code></dt>
      <dd class="ml-6 text-muted-foreground"><p>Set to <code>false</code> if you want to make the OADP controller skip re-running tests.</p></dd>
      <dt class="font-semibold"><code>uploadSpeedTestConfig</code></dt>
      <dd class="ml-6 text-muted-foreground"><p>Configures the upload speed test by setting the <code>fileSize</code> and <code>timeout</code> fields.</p></dd>
      </dl>
      </li>
      <li>
      Create the DPT CR by running the following command:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc create -f <dpt_file_name>"} lang="terminal" />
      <p>Replace <code>&lt;dpt_file_name&gt;</code> with the file name of the DPT manifest.</p>
      </li>
      </ol>
      <p><strong>Verification</strong></p>
      <ol>
      <li>
      Verify that the phase of the DPT CR is <code>Complete</code> by running the following command:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc get dpt dpt-sample"} lang="terminal" />
      <p>The example output is as following:</p>
      <CodeBlock code={"NAME         PHASE      LASTTESTED   UPLOADSPEED(MBPS)   ENCRYPTION   VERSIONING   SNAPSHOTS    AGE\ndpt-sample   Complete   17m          546                 AES256       Enabled      2/2 passed   17m"} lang="terminal" />
      </li>
      <li>
      Verify that the CSI snapshots are ready and the data upload tests are successful by running the following command:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc get dpt dpt-sample -o yaml"} lang="terminal" />
      <p>The example output is as following:</p>
      <CodeBlock code={"apiVersion: oadp.openshift.io/v1alpha1\nkind: DataProtectionTest\n....\nstatus:\n  bucketMetadata:\n    encryptionAlgorithm: AES256\n    versioningStatus: Enabled\n  lastTested: \"202...:47:51Z\"\n  phase: Complete\n  s3Vendor: AWS\n  snapshotSummary: 2/2 passed\n  snapshotTests:\n  - persistentVolumeClaimName: mysql-data\n    persistentVolumeClaimNamespace: ocp-mysql\n    readyDuration: 24s\n    status: Ready\n  - persistentVolumeClaimName: mysql-data1\n    persistentVolumeClaimNamespace: ocp-mysql\n    readyDuration: 40s\n    status: Ready\n  uploadTest:\n    duration: 3.071s\n    speedMbps: 546\n    success: true"} lang="yaml" />
      <p>where:</p>
      <dl class="my-4 space-y-2">
      <dt class="font-semibold"><code>bucketMetadata</code></dt>
      <dd class="ml-6 text-muted-foreground"><p>Specifies the bucket metadata information.</p></dd>
      <dt class="font-semibold"><code>s3Vendor</code></dt>
      <dd class="ml-6 text-muted-foreground"><p>Specifies the S3 bucket vendor.</p></dd>
      <dt class="font-semibold"><code>snapshotSummary</code></dt>
      <dd class="ml-6 text-muted-foreground"><p>Specifies the summary of the CSI snapshot tests.</p></dd>
      <dt class="font-semibold"><code>uploadTest</code></dt>
      <dd class="ml-6 text-muted-foreground"><p>Specifies the upload test details.</p></dd>
      </dl>
      </li>
      </ol>
      <h2 id="oadp-dpt-use-case-bsl-spec_oadp-data-protection-test" class="group scroll-mt-20">Running a data protection test by configuring a backup storage location specification<a href="#oadp-dpt-use-case-bsl-spec_oadp-data-protection-test" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1">&para;</a></h2>
      <p class="_abstract">Configure and run the <code>DataProtectionTest</code> (DPT) custom resource (CR) by specifying an inline backup storage location (BSL) specification instead of referencing an existing BSL name. This helps you test data upload performance and CSI snapshot readiness without creating a separate BSL resource.</p>
      <p><strong>Prerequisites</strong></p>
      <ul>
      <li>You have logged in to the OpenShift Container Platform cluster as a user with the <code>cluster-admin</code> role.</li>
      <li>You have installed the OpenShift CLI (<code>oc</code>).</li>
      <li>You have installed the OADP Operator.</li>
      <li>You have created the <code>DataProtectionApplication</code> (DPA) CR.</li>
      <li>You have configured a bucket to store the backups.</li>
      <li>You have created the <code>Secret</code> object to access the bucket storage.</li>
      <li>You have an application with persistent volume claims (PVCs) running in a separate namespace.</li>
      </ul>
      <p><strong>Procedure</strong></p>
      <ol>
      <li>
      Create a manifest file for the DPT CR as shown in the example:
      <CodeBlock code={"apiVersion: oadp.openshift.io/v1alpha1\nkind: DataProtectionTest\nmetadata:\n  name: dpt-sample\n  namespace: openshift-adp\nspec:\n  backupLocationSpec:\n    provider: aws\n    default: true\n    objectStorage:\n      bucket: sample-bucket\n      prefix: velero\n    config:\n      region: us-east-1\n      profile: \"default\"\n      insecureSkipTLSVerify: \"true\"\n      s3Url: \"https://s3.amazonaws.com/sample-bucket\"\n    credential:\n      name: cloud-credentials\n      key: cloud\n  uploadSpeedTestConfig:\n    fileSize: 50MB\n    timeout: 120s\n  csiVolumeSnapshotTestConfigs:\n    - volumeSnapshotSource:\n        persistentVolumeClaimName: mongo\n        persistentVolumeClaimNamespace: mongo-persistent\n      snapshotClassName: csi-snapclass\n      timeout: 2m\n  forceRun: true\n  skipTLSVerify: true"} lang="yaml" />
      <p>where:</p>
      <dl class="my-4 space-y-2">
      <dt class="font-semibold"><code>backupLocationSpec</code></dt>
      <dd class="ml-6 text-muted-foreground"><p>Configures the BSL spec by specifying details such as the cloud provider.</p></dd>
      <dt class="font-semibold"><code>sample-bucket</code></dt>
      <dd class="ml-6 text-muted-foreground"><p>Specifies the bucket name. In this example, the bucket name is <code>sample-bucket</code>.</p></dd>
      <dt class="font-semibold"><code>us-east-1</code></dt>
      <dd class="ml-6 text-muted-foreground"><p>Specifies the cloud provider region.</p></dd>
      <dt class="font-semibold"><code>credential</code></dt>
      <dd class="ml-6 text-muted-foreground"><p>Specifies the cloud credentials for the storage bucket.</p></dd>
      <dt class="font-semibold"><code>uploadSpeedTestConfig</code></dt>
      <dd class="ml-6 text-muted-foreground"><p>(Optional) Configures the upload speed test by setting the <code>fileSize</code> and <code>timeout</code> fields.</p></dd>
      <dt class="font-semibold"><code>csiVolumeSnapshotTestConfigs</code></dt>
      <dd class="ml-6 text-muted-foreground"><p>Configures the CSI volume snapshot test.</p></dd>
      <dt class="font-semibold"><code>skipTLSVerify</code></dt>
      <dd class="ml-6 text-muted-foreground"><p>Set to <code>true</code> to skip the TLS certificate validation during the DPT CR run.</p></dd>
      </dl>
      </li>
      <li>
      Create the DPT CR by running the following command:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc create -f <dpt_file_name>"} lang="terminal" />
      <p>Replace <code>&lt;dpt_file_name&gt;</code> with the file name of the DPT manifest.</p>
      </li>
      </ol>
      <p><strong>Verification</strong></p>
      <ol>
      <li>
      Verify that the phase of the DPT CR is <code>Complete</code> by running the following command:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc get dpt dpt-sample"} lang="terminal" />
      <p>The example output is as following:</p>
      <CodeBlock code={"NAME         PHASE      LASTTESTED   UPLOADSPEED(MBPS)   ENCRYPTION   VERSIONING   SNAPSHOTS    AGE\ndpt-sample   Complete   17m          546                 AES256       Enabled      2/2 passed   17m"} lang="terminal" />
      </li>
      </ol>
      <h2 id="oadp-dpt-use-case-azure_oadp-data-protection-test" class="group scroll-mt-20">Running a data protection test on an Azure object storage<a href="#oadp-dpt-use-case-azure_oadp-data-protection-test" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1">&para;</a></h2>
      <p class="_abstract">Run the <code>DataProtectionTest</code> (DPT) custom resource (CR) on Azure object storage by configuring the required Azure credentials, including the <code>STORAGE_ACCOUNT_ID</code> parameter in the secret object. This helps you validate your OADP configuration and verify CSI snapshot readiness on Azure clusters.</p>
      <p><strong>Prerequisites</strong></p>
      <ul>
      <li>You have logged in to the Azure cluster as a user with the <code>cluster-admin</code> role.</li>
      <li>You have installed the OpenShift CLI (<code>oc</code>).</li>
      <li>You have installed the OADP Operator.</li>
      <li>You have configured a bucket to store the backups.</li>
      <li>You have an application with persistent volume claims (PVCs) running in a separate namespace.</li>
      </ul>
      <p><strong>Procedure</strong></p>
      <ol>
      <li>
      Add the <code>Storage Blob Data Contributor</code> role to Azure <code>storageAccount</code> object to avoid DPT run failure. Run the following command:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ az role assignment create \\\n--assignee \"$AZURE_CLIENT_ID\" \\\n--role \"Storage Blob Data Contributor\" \\\n--scope \"/subscriptions/$AZURE_SUBSCRIPTION_ID/resourceGroups/$AZURE_RESOURCE_GROUP/providers/Microsoft.Storage/storageAccounts/$AZURE_STORAGE_ACCOUNT_ID\""} lang="terminal" />
      </li>
      <li>
      In your terminal, export the Azure parameters and create a secret credentials file with the parameters as shown in the following example.
      <p>To run the DPT CR on Azure, you need to specify the <code>STORAGE_ACCOUNT_ID</code> parameter in the secret credentials file.</p>
      <CodeBlock code={"AZURE_SUBSCRIPTION_ID=<subscription_id>\nAZURE_TENANT_ID=<tenant_id>\nAZURE_CLIENT_ID=<client_id>\nAZURE_CLIENT_SECRET=<client_secret>\nAZURE_RESOURCE_GROUP=<resource_group>\nAZURE_STORAGE_ACCOUNT_ID=<storage_account>"} lang="terminal" />
      </li>
      <li>
      Create the <code>Secret</code> CR as shown in the following example:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc create secret generic cloud-credentials-azure -n openshift-adp --from-file cloud=<credentials_file_path>"} lang="terminal" />
      </li>
      <li>
      Create the <code>DataProtectionApplication</code> (DPA) CR by using the configuration shown in the following example:
      <CodeBlock code={"apiVersion: oadp.openshift.io/v1alpha1\nkind: DataProtectionApplication\nmetadata:\n  name: ts-dpa\n  namespace: openshift-adp \nspec:\n  configuration:\n    velero:\n      defaultPlugins:\n        - azure\n        - openshift \n  backupLocations:\n    - velero:\n        config:\n          resourceGroup: oadp-....-b7q4-rg\n          storageAccount: oadp...kb7q4\n          subscriptionId: 53b8f5...fd54c8a\n        credential:\n          key: cloud\n          name: cloud-credentials-azure\n        provider: azure\n        default: true\n        objectStorage:\n          bucket: <bucket_name>\n          prefix: velero"} lang="yaml" />
      <p>Replace <code>name</code> with the name of the <code>Secret</code> object. In this example, the name is <code>cloud-credentials-azure</code>.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
      Create the DPT CR by specifying the name of backup storage location (BSL), <code>VolumeSnapshotClass</code> object, and the persistent volume claim details as shown in the following example:
      <CodeBlock code={"apiVersion: oadp.openshift.io/v1alpha1\nkind: DataProtectionTest\nmetadata:\n  name: dpt-sample\n  namespace: openshift-adp\nspec:\n  backupLocationName: <bsl_name>\n  uploadSpeedTestConfig:\n    fileSize: 40MB\n    timeout: 120s\n  csiVolumeSnapshotTestConfigs:\n    - snapshotClassName: csi-azuredisk-vsc\n      timeout: 90s\n      volumeSnapshotSource:\n        persistentVolumeClaimName: mysql-data\n        persistentVolumeClaimNamespace: ocp-mysql\n    - snapshotClassName: csi-azuredisk-vsc\n      timeout: 120s\n      volumeSnapshotSource:\n        persistentVolumeClaimName: mysql-data1\n        persistentVolumeClaimNamespace: ocp-mysql"} lang="yaml" />
      <p>where:</p>
      <dl class="my-4 space-y-2">
      <dt class="font-semibold"><code>&lt;bsl_name&gt;</code></dt>
      <dd class="ml-6 text-muted-foreground"><p>Specifies the name of the BSL.</p></dd>
      <dt class="font-semibold"><code>csi-azuredisk-vsc</code></dt>
      <dd class="ml-6 text-muted-foreground"><p>Specifies the Azure snapshot class name.</p></dd>
      <dt class="font-semibold"><code>mysql-data</code></dt>
      <dd class="ml-6 text-muted-foreground"><p>Specifies the name of the persistent volume claim.</p></dd>
      <dt class="font-semibold"><code>ocp-mysql</code></dt>
      <dd class="ml-6 text-muted-foreground"><p>Specifies the name of the persistent volume claim namespace.</p></dd>
      </dl>
      </li>
      <li>Run the DPT CR to verify the snapshot readiness.</li>
      </ol>
      <h2 id="oadp-troubleshooting-dpt_oadp-data-protection-test" class="group scroll-mt-20">Troubleshooting the DataProtectionTest custom resource<a href="#oadp-troubleshooting-dpt_oadp-data-protection-test" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1">&para;</a></h2>
      <p class="_abstract">Troubleshoot common <code>DataProtectionTest</code> (DPT) custom resource (CR) issues, such as stuck progress states, upload test failures, and snapshot test failures. This helps you identify and resolve problems with your DPT configuration.</p>
      <p><strong>DPT CR troubleshooting</strong></p>
      <Table class="my-4">
      <TableHeader>
      <TableRow>
      <TableHead>Error</TableHead>
      <TableHead>Reason</TableHead>
      <TableHead>Solution</TableHead>
      </TableRow>
      </TableHeader>
      <TableBody>
      <TableRow>
      <TableCell>DPT stuck in <code>InProgress</code> state</TableCell>
      <TableCell>Bucket credentials or bucket access failure</TableCell>
      <TableCell>Check <code>Secret</code> object, bucket permissions, and logs.</TableCell>
      </TableRow>
      <TableRow>
      <TableCell>Upload test failed</TableCell>
      <TableCell>Incorrect <code>Secret</code> object or S3 endpoint</TableCell>
      <TableCell>Check the <code>BackupStorageLocation</code> object config and the access keys.</TableCell>
      </TableRow>
      <TableRow>
      <TableCell>Snapshot tests fail</TableCell>
      <TableCell>Incorrect configuration of CSI snapshot controller</TableCell>
      <TableCell>Check the <code>VolumeSnapshotClass</code> object availability and the CSI driver logs.</TableCell>
      </TableRow>
      <TableRow>
      <TableCell>Bucket encryption or versioning not populated</TableCell>
      <TableCell>Cloud provider limitations</TableCell>
      <TableCell>Not all object storage providers expose these fields consistently.</TableCell>
      </TableRow>
      </TableBody>
      </Table>
    </article>
